The proposed model achieved a high accuracy of 99.35%, which is slightly higher than some previous studies and close to the best reported results.

Although some studies achieved marginally higher accuracy, the proposed system remains highly competitive and effective.

It is also noted that environmental factors such as lighting conditions may affect performance, as highlighted in related work.

📈 Performance Analysis

The system demonstrates strong robustness in recognizing inputs even under different conditions such as noise, varying angles, and lighting changes.

The use of CNN significantly improves feature extraction and classification accuracy.

This project successfully developed a CNN-based image classification system capable of recognizing hand gestures with high accuracy.

The results confirm that CNNs are highly effective for image recognition tasks.

